/* Blocking factors for the GEMM kernel.
 * These values are chosen to fit reasonably well in the L1/L2 caches
 * on modern x86-64 CPUs. They are kept small and conservative to work
 * well across a range of architectures, and they safely handle any
 * problem size via edge handling in the loops.
 *
